Subject: ggml-vulkan: try wider G17S single-token K-quant workgroups

For dense Q4_K/Q6_K matrix-vector work with long inner dimensions, try
splitting the inner product across four subgroups using the existing
hybrid reduction. Match the real G17S identity from the prefill patch.
Do not select this for MoE, batched GEMM, integer-dot, or other GPUs.

--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
@@ -5898,6 +5898,10 @@
 
     // heuristic to choose workgroup size
     uint32_t dmmv_wg = DMMV_WG_SIZE_SUBGROUP;
+    if (ctx->device->borealis_g17s && num_cols == 1 && k >= 1024 && m <= 8192 &&
+        b_type != GGML_TYPE_Q8_1 && (a_type == GGML_TYPE_Q4_K || a_type == GGML_TYPE_Q6_K)) {
+        dmmv_wg = DMMV_WG_SIZE_LARGE;
+    }
     if ((ctx->device->vendor_id == VK_VENDOR_ID_NVIDIA && ctx->device->architecture != vk_device_architecture::NVIDIA_PRE_TURING) || ctx->device->vendor_id == VK_VENDOR_ID_INTEL) {
         // Prefer larger workgroups when M is small, to spread the work out more
         // and keep more SMs busy.
